== Core Mechanic Terms

*3d6:* The core dice roll. Three six-sided dice, summed, plus modifiers.

*Always Hit:* Attacks do not roll to hit, the 3d6 determines damage tier. Every attack connects. Every swing matters.

*Attribute:* One of six core stats: Brawn, Fortitude, Agility, Guile, Knowledge, Reason. Ranges from -2 to +2.

*Bell Curve:* The probability distribution of 3d6. Most rolls cluster around 9–12. Extreme results (3 and 18) are rare, about 0.5% each.

*Boon:* Roll 4d6 and keep the highest three. A second step rolls 5d6 kept three, a third rolls 6d6 kept three, and three steps is the ceiling. Boons and Banes cancel one for one. Halflings get a boon once per session from their Lucky trait.

*Bane:* Roll 4d6 and keep the _lowest_ three. The opposite of a boon, and it steps up the same way. Applied by the DA for severe disadvantage.

*Critical:* Three natural 6s on 3d6. Automatic Strong success plus a bonus effect from the Critical table. About a 1 in 216 chance.

*Fumble:* Three natural 1s on 3d6. Automatic failure plus a complication. About a 1 in 216 chance. The table groans.

*Success Tier:* The three bands of outcome: Weak (1-8), Standard (9-14), Strong (15-18+). Every roll lands in one of these.

*Weak:* Partial success or success with complication. You get what you wanted, barely, or at a cost.

*Standard:* Full, clean success. The thing you attempted works as intended.

*Strong:* Exceptional success. Extra effect, bonus damage, additional information, or sheer style.

*Damage Budget:* The master table every damaging spell, ability, and maneuver keys to. Novice 4/6/8, Adept 5/8/11, Master 7/10/14 (Weak/Standard/Strong). See @sec-damage-budget

*Flat Damage:* Damage taken straight from the damage budget row with no attribute added. Arrows, thrown attacks, most spells, and all monsters use flat damage.

*Attribute-Scaled Damage:* Damage that adds the card's stated attribute to a base value, minimum 1 damage. Novice cards use the Basic-card floor (1/2/3). Adept and Master cards use the budget row minus 3 (2/5/8 and 4/7/11). Melee attack cards add Brawn (or Agility for Finesse). Missile and thrown attacks are flat, no attribute added.

