== Character Terms

*Ability:* An active power purchased with DP. Spells, combat techniques, and signature class powers are all abilities. Must be activated to use. Bought at one tier, Novice, Adept, or Master, for a flat DP cost by tier.

*Ancestry:* Your species, Human, Elf, Dwarf, or Halfling. Grants one Discipline and one trait.

*Background:* Level 0. Your hero's life before adventuring. Governed by Background DP (8 + Knowledge + Fortitude).

*Carry Slots:* How much you can carry: 10 + (Brawn x 5), floor 5. Most items take 1 slot, armor takes 2 to 4, and two-handed weapons take 2. See *Encumbrance*.

*Class:* Your hero's calling, Protector, Blade, Arcanist, Shepherd, Intellect, Odd, Leader, Unbalanced, or Shadow. Determines favored skills, favored Disciplines, and signature ability.

*Culture:* Your upbringing within your ancestry. Grants a +1 skill bonus and either two specific Disciplines or one free Discipline.

*Development Points (DP):* The currency of character creation and advancement. Spent to purchase skills, abilities, and Disciplines. Skills and abilities cost a flat rate by tier (Novice 2 DP, Adept 4 DP, Master 8 DP). Disciplines cost different amounts per class depending on their cost structure (Home, Adjacent, Foreign, Opposed).

*Discipline:* A prerequisite resource representing mastery of a domain. Disciplines come in types: Elemental (Fire, Earth, Wind, Water), Weapon (Blades, Axes, Polearms, Heavy Weapon, Archery, Unarmed), Defense (Protection, Armor), Primal (Animal, Plants), Arcane (Energy), Divine (Life, Religion), Esoteric (Mind, Summon, Fate), Subterfuge (Stealth, Sleight), and Knowledge (Lore, Tactics). Each class has a cost table showing the DP price for each rank in each discipline (see @sec-chapter-classes).

*Wildcard Rank:* A single rank held by the Odd that stands in for any one Discipline. It is never assigned, it satisfies one requirement of one rank at a time, it never advances, and it costs no Development Points. See @sec-chapter-classes

*HP (Health Points):* How much damage you can take before falling unconscious. Starting HP = 10 + Fortitude + Knowledge. Your HP does not increase with level; your Grit does.

*Encumbrance:* The slot system for the gear you carry. Slots are Carry Slots; one container at a time is exempt from them, and containers cannot be nested inside one another. See *Carry Slots*.

*Kit:* Your hero's outfit: one option from each of the four lines, Armament, Covering, Focus, and Calling, bought with six kit points. A kit adds no numbers to your sheet. It grants permissions, the fiction of what you brought, and points left over for packs. See @sec-chapter-equipment

*Kit Point:* The currency of the kit. Six at creation, plus one from a class's granted pack or from a talent that grants kit. Leftover points buy packs, one point each.

*Pack:* A capability you carry, bought with a leftover kit point, such as the `climbing` pack or the `healer` pack. Every hero also has the free Adventurer's Pack. A pack is what you brought, not a shopping list.

*Level:* Your hero's experience tier, from 1 to 10. Higher levels unlock Adept (Level 3) and Master (Level 7) abilities and grant attribute increases every 4 levels.

*Novice:* The first tier of any skill or ability. Grants +1 bonus. Flat cost: 2 DP.

*Adept:* The second tier. For a skill, the +2 bonus. Flat cost: 4 DP. Unlocks at Level 3.

*Master:* The third tier. For a skill, the +3 bonus. Flat cost: 8 DP. Unlocks at Level 7.

*Rank:* A single step of a Discipline, from 1 to 3. A card names the Discipline ranks it needs, and those ranks are its own prerequisite. The card's tier sets the level it needs (Novice 1, Adept 3, Master 7). A hero's maximum in any single Discipline is 3 ranks.

*Signature Ability:* The unique power granted by your class at Level 1. Defines your class identity mechanically.

*Eccentric Spellcasting:* The Odd's signature ability. Choose one arcane ability and one divine ability; you ignore prerequisite Disciplines for these two (level requirements still apply) and need no arcane focus or holy symbol.

*Skill:* A trained competency. Ranges from Novice (+1) to Master (+3). Includes physical skills (Athletics), knowledge skills (Arcana), social skills (Persuasion), and subterfuge skills (Stealth).

*Talent:* A benefit purchased with DP. Most are always on and need no activation; some are activated talents, and the card's Action field says which. Examples: Tough (+2 HP), Fortune's Favor (spend a Reaction to reroll one natural 1, 2, or 3, once per session).

*Trait:* An ancestry-granted special ability. Human: Versatile. Elf: Elven Grace. Dwarf: Sturdy. Halfling: Lucky.

