== Magic Terms

*Spell:* A magical ability bought as a spell card. Always fires, no spell slots, no mana.

*Cantrip:* The minor spells every caster of a tradition knows without buying them. Cantrips carry no Discipline requirement and cost no DP, and their damage line is 1/3/5, deliberately below the Novice row.

*Spell Card:* A spell in the standard card format. A Novice spell card prints Weak, Standard, and Strong outcomes; an Adept or Master spell is a separate card with its own name and a single effect. There are no spell chains.

*Concentration Spell:* A spell that requires ongoing focus, and you can maintain only one at a time. If you take damage while concentrating, make a Fortitude check: Standard or better on 3d6 + Fortitude holds the spell together, and you make that check again each time damage lands on you.

*Arcane Focus:* An item (wand, staff, orb) that channels arcane magic. A spell whose card carries `focus:arcane` in its Kit field requires one.

*Holy Symbol:* An item (amulet, reliquary, sacred text) that channels divine magic. A spell whose card carries `focus:holy` in its Kit field requires one.

*Attunement:* The bond between a hero and a magic item. Maximum 3 attuned items at a time. Artifacts, unique items of legend beyond even Legendary rarity, don't count against this limit.

*Magic Item Card:* A named, unique magic item that grants a maneuver, an action, or a passive benefit. Magic items are found, not bought, and have no price. Actions granted by a magic item roll with the user's attributes.

