== GM Terms

*DA (Dungeon Architect):* The game master. Runs the world, plays the NPCs, adjudicates the rules.

*Challenge:* A penalty the DA applies to your roll when the world or an opponent opposes you. A goblin might be -1 (barely a threat) and a dragon -6 (good luck), and the DA tells you the number before you roll. A monster's stat block prints the same number as a positive rating, so a Challenge 3 knight imposes -3 on your roll. See @sec-chapter-core-resolution

*Challenge ½ (C½):* The minion-tier Challenge rating. Creatures at Challenge ½ (goblins, bandits, cultists) are individually weak and meant to be fought in numbers.

*Difficulty Modifier:* A bonus or penalty the DA applies to a roll based on how hard the task is. Ranges from +4 (Trivial) to -6 (Nearly Impossible).

*Passive Insight:* A creature's baseline ability to detect lies and hidden threats. Calculated as Knowledge score + 7.

*Recharge:* A monster ability usable again when the DA rolls 1d6 at the start of the monster's turn and gets a 5–6.

*Respite:* A full night's rest. Grit returns on a respite, and nothing shorter brings it back.

*Rest:* Time taken to recover. A short rest takes 1 hour and has no default mechanical effect. A long rest takes 8 hours and provides the full recovery benefits (see @sec-chapter-gm-guidance).

*Session:* One gaming session, typically 3–4 hours. Some abilities refresh per session.

*Encounter:* A single scene or combat. Some abilities refresh per encounter.

*Campaign:* The entire ongoing story, spanning multiple sessions and potentially years of play.
